.TH CCLIVE 1 "2026-11-09" "atelier instruments" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cclive \- what any session on this machine is doing, holding or claimed on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cclive
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR dir ]...
.RB [ \-\-fresh
.IR minutes ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B cclive
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work is coordinated repo by repo: a claim on one board, a worktree in one
checkout, a session in one directory.
A session that opens one repo cannot otherwise learn that another session is
mid-flight in a sibling, even where the two could coordinate over a shared
credential, host or subject.
.PP
.B cclive
gives one view of live work across the repos on this machine, grouped by repo
with a total, to be read at session open.
It prints the time and the load average, the roots it scanned and what it
skipped, one line of totals, a section for each repo with anything in it, one
line naming the quiet repos, and the limits.
.SS What it reads
Everything it reads was written for another reason, and it writes nothing:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRepos\fR: one level under each search root, a directory with a
.I .git
entry.
A linked worktree found there is skipped, and is read through its own repo.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBClaims\fR: the board's
.B [~]
lines at the newest of the repo's
.BR main ", " master ", " origin/main " and " origin/master .
The claim commit reaches those refs; the working tree may be on another branch
or behind.
A board with a generated index is read from its item store, a hand-kept
.I ROADMAP.md
from that file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWorktrees\fR:
.BR "git worktree list" ,
with the age of each one's last commit.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLive sessions\fR: transcripts under
.I ~/.claude/projects
written in the last ten minutes (\fB\-\-fresh\fR changes the bound), and the
agent transcripts of sessions active in the last day.
The tail of a fresh transcript gives its working directory, branch and title;
transcripts are never read whole.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLoad\fR: the 1, 5 and 15 minute load averages and the core count.
.SS What counts as a claim
A left-margin
.B [~]
line, or an indented
.B [~]
line carrying a claim stamp.
A stamp may sit on any line of the item's first paragraph.
A claim with a stamp is \fIdated\fR and shows its age, worktree and session;
a left-margin
.B [~]
with no stamp is \fIundated\fR and is counted, and listed only with
.BR \-\-all .
An indented
.B [~]
with no stamp is a progress mark on a sub-bullet and is not counted.
.SS Live and quiet
A session is listed under the repo its own working directory is in, matched to
the longest worktree path of any scanned repo.
A subagent is matched by its own directory, so an orchestrator in one repo
with a worker in another shows in both.
A session in no scanned repo is listed under
.BR elsewhere .
.PP
A claim is marked
.B live
when its stamp names a live session or a worktree with a live session in it.
A worktree is marked
.B live
when a live session is in it or a live claim names it.
Anything else is marked
.BR quiet ,
which means only that no such match was found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " dir"
A directory whose children are the repos.
Repeatable.
Default: the colon-separated
.B $CCLIVE_ROOTS
if set, otherwise the parent directory of this atelier checkout.
The header says which it used.
.TP
.BI \-\-fresh " minutes"
A transcript counts as live if written this recently.
Default ten, the bound
.BR ccclose (1)
uses, from a census of agent logs.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Lift the caps: every claim and worktree, undated claims too, and every skipped
name.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
Every field is present on every repo; lists are never capped.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
A one-screen summary.
.SH OUTPUT
Every repo section starts with the same fields in the same order.
A known zero is printed.
An unknown prints as
.B ?
with its reason: a repo with no board shows
.BR "claims ?" ,
never
.BR "claims 0" ,
and is starred in the quiet line.
.PP
Claims and worktrees are capped at five per repo and the cut is counted.
Sessions are never capped.
Repos with a live session come first, then by newest commit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The view printed, including a partial one that says what it could not read.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage, or neither a search root nor the transcript store could be read.
.SH LIMITS
.IP \(bu 2
A claim is a commit, so a stale claim looks live.
It stays until a commit removes it, whether or not its session survived.
.IP \(bu 2
A quiet transcript might be a slow agent, past the bound on one long command.
A session open and waiting on its operator writes nothing and reads as quiet,
while still holding its worktree.
.IP \(bu 2
Another machine's sessions are invisible.
Only this machine's transcripts are read, and nothing is fetched, so a claim
pushed from elsewhere shows only once a fetch has brought it here.
.IP \(bu 2
Only repos under the roots are scanned.
.IP \(bu 2
A subagent still writing a day after its parent's last write is not seen.
Of 3,602 agent logs measured, none wrote more than 0.2 hours past the parent.
.IP \(bu 2
Open pull requests, dirty state and running processes are not read.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/*/<session>.jsonl
Session transcripts, read by modification time and a bounded tail.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/*/<session>/subagents/agent\-*.jsonl
Agent transcripts, likewise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CCLIVE_ROOTS
Colon-separated search roots, used when no
.B \-\-root
is given.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID
Marks the session running the tool in the view.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cclive
The view, at session open.
.TP
.B cclive \-\-fresh 60
Everyone active in the past hour.
.TP
.B cclive \-\-json | jq \(aq.totals\(aq
The totals, for a tool.
.SH NOTES
The design of record is
.IR instruments/cclive.design.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccclose (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
